+//  isolate controls) while `[C]` / `[T]` / `[K]` ios were OK: the marker is
+//  then wrapped in a pair of strong MARKS — LRM U+200E … LRM (ltr item) or
+//  RLM U+200F … RLM (rtl item) — instead of LRI/RLI … PDI. UAX #9 P2 then
+//  finds the item's direction at once, and the trailing mark keeps a final
+//  neutral (the `.` of `א.`) between two strong characters of the item's
